# ScriptedController.ChooseTargets (control.go) never validates its queued
# answer against the candidates it was offered, unlike a real player's UI or
# the AI -- this scenario uses that to isolate the CR 608.2b re-check
# (targetStillLegal -> cardCantBeTargetedBy) on its own, a target Java could
# never actually have chosen. TestTargetCandidates* (staticability_internal_test.go)
# holds the choice-time filter (targetCandidates) to the same rule directly.
# CR 702.11b/e: Hexproof only refuses an opponent's spell or ability, its
# own Activator$ Opponent gate (cardCantBeTargetedBy, staticability.go).
# ai's own players are still a legal candidate for Lightning Bolt's own
# ValidTgts$ Any (targetCandidates never returns an empty set here), so
# casting still succeeds; the CR 608.2b re-check at resolution
# (targetStillLegal) then finds human's Rubbleback Rhino illegal and drops
# it, the only target Bolt named -- Bolt fizzles, dealing no damage.
startturn ai
advance 3
tapformana ai 2 R
queue targets 1
queue action ai cast 3
passpriority
